1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,903
The same constant governs electrolysis.

2
00:00:02,903 --> 00:00:09,986
Faraday's first law: the mass deposited is proportional to the charge passed, current times time.

3
00:00:09,986 --> 00:00:15,833
His second law: the same charge deposits masses in the ratio of their equivalent weights.

4
00:00:15,833 --> 00:00:22,981
In practice, one faraday deposits one gram equivalent, molar mass over n grams.

